#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:2
msgid "RSGP Solar System Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:5
msgid ""
"The solar system simulation serves as the source of power within the "
"system. This chapter examines the implementation of photovoltaic panel "
"modeling, battery energy storage systems, and inverter control mechanisms"
" that enable realistic solar power generation and management."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:7
msgid ""
"While the houses simulation models energy consumption, the solar system "
"simulation models energy production and storage. Together they form the "
"fundamental supply-demand dynamic that defines smart grids. The power "
"management system, discussed in later chapters, coordinates between these"
" two to optimize energy usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:10
msgid "Solar System Architecture Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:11
msgid ""
"The solar system simulation architecture consists of photovoltaic panels,"
" one battery, and an inverter connecting the elements. The inverter is "
"then connected to the power manager through a load line and a utility "
"line. This design separates concerns between energy generation, storage, "
"and power conversion and enables more realistic modeling of each "
"component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:17
msgid ""
"The **Panels** handle solar irradiance calculations and power generation "
"based on the data collected from the National Solar Radiation Database "
"(NSRDB). The **Battery** manages charge state tracking. The **Inverter** "
"adheres to its operational mode control and manages power distribution "
"from and to the solar system components and the demands of the power "
"manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:19
msgid ""
"The three-component architecture enables independent development and "
"testing of solar generation, energy storage, and power distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:22
msgid "Photovoltaic Panel Modeling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:23
msgid ""
"The photovoltaic panels integrate with the National Solar Radiation "
"Database to obtain weather information and employs the PVLib photovoltaic"
" modeling library to perform accurate solar calculations. The panel model"
" accounts for solar position, atmospheric conditions, and system "
"configuration parameters to generate power output that mirror actual "
"photovoltaic system performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:29
msgid ""
"The NSRDB contains hourly solar irradiance measurements, temperature "
"data, and atmospheric conditions for locations across the United States. "
"In the simulation, only data local to Phoenix/Arizona was used. The "
"simulation system processes this data to extract direct normal irradiance"
" (DNI), diffuse horizontal irradiance (DHI), and global horizontal "
"irradiance (GHI) values necessary for photovoltaic calculations. The "
"database integration includes automatic timestamp conversion, timezone "
"handling, and data interpolation to support accelerated simulation time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:31
msgid ""
"Solar position calculations account for latitude, longitude, time of "
"year, and time of day to determine solar azimuth and elevation angles. "
"The solar position information combines with irradiance data (DNI, DHI, "
"and GHI) to calculate the effective solar energy. The PVLib library "
"performs these calculations using established solar position algorithms. "
"Below is an overview of the parameters of that calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:37
msgid "Components of solar radiation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:39
msgid ""
"**Direct Normal Irradiance (DNI)** represents the irradiance directly "
"from the sun to the surface of the photovoltaic panels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:41
msgid ""
"**Diffuse Horizontal Irradiance(DHI)** represents the irradiance "
"indirectly reaching the surface of the photovoltaic panels through the "
"rays scattered by the sky dome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:43
msgid ""
"**Global Horizontal Irradiance(GHI)** represents the total irradiance, "
"calculated by the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:45
msgid "GHI = DNI \\times \\cos(\\theta) + DHI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:49
msgid "where :math:`\\theta` is the solar zenith angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:54
msgid "Solar zenith angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:56
msgid ""
"The simulation supports configurable panel count, individual panel area, "
"and conversion efficiency specifications that determine total array "
"capacity. The total photovoltaic power generation follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:58
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P_{total} = POA_{irradiance} \\times A_{panel} \\times \\eta_{panel} "
"\\times N_{panels}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:62
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`POA_{irradiance}` represents plane-of-array irradiance, "
":math:`A_{panel}` represents individual panel area, :math:`\\eta_{panel}`"
" represents panel efficiency, and :math:`N_{panels}` represents the "
"number of panels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:65
msgid "Battery Energy Storage System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:66
msgid ""
"The battery system implement lithium-ion battery characteristics "
"including charge acceptance, storage capacity, and charge efficiency. The"
" model provides an interface to the inverter to charge and discharge from"
" the battery as per its calculations. As such, the battery component "
"itself is devoid of any calculations beside implementing its charge "
"efficiency and limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:68
msgid "The battery charge operation follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:70
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P_{charge,actual} = \\min(P_{charge,requested}, P_{max,charge}) \\times "
"\\eta_{charge}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:74
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E_{charge} = P_{charge,actual} \\times \\Delta t"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:78
#, python-brace-format
msgid "SoC_{new} = \\min(SoC_{current} + E_{charge}, C_{total})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:82
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\eta_{charge}` represents charging efficiency, "
":math:`\\Delta t` time interval in hours (:math:`\\Delta t = "
"\\frac{\\Delta t_{s}}{3600}` where :math:`\\Delta t_{s}` is the interval "
"in seconds), and :math:`SoC` state-of-charge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:84
msgid ""
"The battery can also be configured on the maximum charge current it can "
"accept, and the maximum discharge. This models the safety considerations "
"present in actual batteries as they reject currents above a certain "
"level. The discharge operation implements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:86
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P_{discharge,actual} = \\min(P_{discharge,requested}, P_{max,discharge}) "
"/ \\eta_{charge}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:90
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"E_{discharge} = \\min(P_{discharge,actual} \\times \\Delta t, "
"SoC_{current})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:94
#, python-brace-format
msgid "SoC_{new} = SoC_{current} - E_{discharge}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:99
msgid "Inverter Control System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:100
msgid ""
"The inverter manages power flow between the photovoltaic panels, battery,"
" and the power manager. It implements DC to AC conversion modeling to "
"account for power losses that occur when converting direct current from "
"the photovoltaic panels and the battery to alternating current for load "
"consumption and utility export. The conversion is handled by the PVWatts "
"library that follows established algorithms to accurately model the "
"conversion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:102
msgid "The DC to AC conversion follows the PVWatts model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:104
msgid ""
"P_{ac} = \\min\\left(\\eta_{inv} \\times P_{dc} \\times \\left(1 - "
"\\frac{P_{dc}}{P_{dc0}}\\right), P_{ac0}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:108
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\eta_{inv}` represents inverter efficiency, :math:`P_{dc0}`"
" represents DC power rating, and :math:`P_{ac0}` represents AC power "
"rating. The reverse calculation for required DC power uses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:110
msgid "P_{dc,required} = \\frac{P_{ac,target}}{\\eta_{inv,overall}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:114
msgid "The inverter implements three operating modes for power flow priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:116
msgid ""
"**Solar-Battery-Utility (SBU) mode** prioritizes using the power "
"available from the photovoltaic panels if present, and only when the "
"panels by themselves do not meet the load that it draws from the battery."
" When the battery is empty, only then would the inverter draw from "
"utility. This mode aims to reduce grid-dependency to a minimum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:118
msgid ""
"**Solar-Utility-Battery (SUB) mode** prioritizes using the power "
"available from the photovoltaic panels--just like the previous mode. "
"However, when the panels power prove insufficient, it draws from utility "
"to meet the demand and keeps the battery as only a last resort when no "
"other source of energy exists. This mode aims to provide security and "
"prepare to meet emergencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:120
msgid ""
"**Utility-Solar-Battery (USB) mode** prioritizes drawing from utility. It"
" uses the solar system as only a back-up in case the utility is out of "
"service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:122
msgid ""
"The power manager can switch the operation mode of the inverter. This may"
" prove useful in scenarios where the battery should be reserved for a "
"foreseen emergency, thus switching the operation mode to SUB to use the "
"utility now and keep the battery to be used when neither the solar panels"
" nor the utility can provide power. While the capability for this "
"currently exists in the system, the power manager carries out no such "
"switches as it currently lacks the ability to predict emergencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:124
msgid ""
"Additionally, the inverter implements a charge priority, which determines"
" how excess solar power gets allocated between battery charging and "
"utility export. The system supports multiple charge priority settings "
"including solar-only charging, solar-first charging, and utility-assisted"
" charging modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:126
msgid ""
"**Solar-only** directs all excess solar power to battery charging before "
"any utility export occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:128
msgid ""
"**Solar-first** uses the excess solar power to charge the battery when "
"present. When not present, it uses the utility to charge the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:130
msgid ""
"**Utility-assisted** enables battery charging from utility power even "
"when some excess solar power is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:132
msgid ""
"In all charge priorities, the inverter will export to utility only when "
"the battery is full. The power flow priority algorithms implement "
"sequential decision trees:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:134
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{remaining} = P_{load} - \\sum_{source} P_{source,allocated}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:138
msgid ""
"where power sources are allocated according to the configured priority "
"mode, and any remaining unmet load triggers load line disconnection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:140
msgid ""
"The inverter implements load shedding as a protective measure that "
"prevents system overload. It disconnects the load when available power "
"sources prove insufficient. The load is then automatically reconnected "
"after a set period of time, during which the power manager should have "
"taken care of the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:142
msgid ""
"The power manager ensures that load shedding may not happen as it "
"automatically disconnects loads from the specific houses that are "
"overusing. As such, load shedding is only ever triggered in the extreme "
"situations where the power manager fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:145
msgid "Weather Data Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:146
msgid ""
"This component manages the interface between the simulation environment "
"and the external weather database, ensuring that solar calculations "
"reflect actual atmospheric conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:148
msgid ""
"The National Solar Radiation Database is the primary data source for "
"solar irradiance and atmospheric conditions. The NSRDB provides hourly "
"measurements of solar radiation components (DNI, DHI, and GHI), ambient "
"temperature, wind speed, and other meteorological parameters collected at"
" numerous locations across the United States. This database is one of the"
" most comprehensive sources of solar data available for renewable energy "
"applications, providing the data necessary for detailed photovoltaic "
"system modeling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:150
msgid ""
"The dataset used from NSRDB covers the aforementioned measurements taken "
"in the Phoenix/Arizona for one full year; one record each half an hour. "
"Data is extracted using the simulation time; the record with the "
"timestamp closest to the current simulation timestamp is used for the "
"calculations of the solar energy in that specific moment in the "
"simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:155
msgid "Snapshot of the NSRDB dataset used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:158
msgid "Power Management Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:159
msgid ""
"The solar system takes in the load from the power manager and gives back "
"the solar panel power used, battery discharged, and grid import or "
"export. The power manager then uses these data to take decisions "
"regarding the load. The interface is two-way; the power manager provides "
"the load, and the solar system provides metrics specifying how the load "
"is being met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:161
msgid ""
"Currently, the interface consists purely of the exchange of data; there "
"is no exchange of commands or requests between the components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:164
msgid "Data Collection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:165
msgid ""
"Data collection operates continuously throughout simulation to capture "
"time-series data about solar generation, battery operation, and system-"
"wide energy flows. The collected data can then be analyzed to pinpoint "
"issues in the model and help refine both the simulation and the power "
"management solutions. Utility import and export represent the most "
"important metrics collected, as they are direct metrics of the "
"effectiveness of the power management solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:167
msgid ""
"The system captures data from all the components to enable any form of "
"analysis. The data collection is extensive: state-of-charge of the "
"battery, power generated from the panels, the system-wide load, utility "
"import and export, among other metrics. The data is logged to a CSV file "
"continuously throughout the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:172
msgid ""
"Plot of solar power generated over time using data collected from the "
"simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:174
msgid ""
"Along the data from NSRDB, the logged CSV files provide all the data "
"needed to carry out analysis on the trends of power generation and "
"consumption. Trend analysis might lead to improvements on the power "
"management solutions. Additionally, AI techniques can be used to benefit "
"from the data and extend the power manager with AI capabilities. This "
"could be especially useful to predict shortages of power generation and "
"thus switch the operation mode of the inverter to import from utility to "
"keep the battery for that shortage and thus maintain long-term system "
"stability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:4
msgid "RSGP Power Management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:8
msgid ""
"The power management system serves as the intelligent coordination layer."
" This chapter examines the algorithms and mathematical foundation that "
"enable the power manager to achieve efficient energy utilization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:10
msgid ""
"The power manager implements an adaptive algorithm that learns from the "
"consumption patterns and adjusts distribution weights as to minimize "
"utility grid dependence. The system operates through two primary "
"components: the central ``PowerManager`` that coordinates system-wide "
"decisions, and individual ``VirtualBattery`` instances that represent "
"each house's allocation within the shared battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:13
msgid "System Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:14
msgid ""
"The power management system integrates with both the houses simulation "
"and solar system simulation through well-defined interfaces that enable "
"real-time coordination and control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:55
msgid ""
"The power manager operates on a configurable update cycle, typically set "
"to match the houses simulation update interval of 100 milliseconds. "
"During each update cycle, the manager executes a sequence of coordinated "
"algorithms that process current system state, update virtual battery "
"parameters, and make power distribution decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:57
msgid ""
"The coordination interface provides bidirectional communication between "
"components. The houses simulation provides current load demands and "
"accepts load line control commands. The solar system simulation provides "
"generation data, battery state information, and accepts load requirements"
" while returning actual power delivery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:60
msgid "Virtual Battery System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:61
msgid ""
"The virtual battery system partitions the shared physical battery among "
"individual houses based on their consumption patterns. Each house "
"receives a dedicated ``VirtualBattery`` instance that tracks its "
"allocated capacity, manages charge and discharge, and tracks the house's "
"weight that determines its share of the total system capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:64
msgid "Mathematical Foundation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:65
msgid ""
"The virtual battery allocation system employs several mathematical "
"relationships to ensure fair and efficient energy distribution. The "
"fundamental relationship establishes the connection between virtual "
"battery capacity and system-wide resources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:67
msgid "C_{vb,i} = \\frac {C_{total}}{N} \\times w_i"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:71
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:95
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:109
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:175
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:247
msgid "where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:73
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{vb,i}` represents the total capacity of virtual battery *i*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:75
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{total}` represents the total capacity of the physical battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:77
msgid "`N` represents the number of houses in the system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:79
msgid "`w_i` represents the weight assigned to house *i*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:81
msgid ""
"The weight constraint ensures that the sum of all virtual capacities "
"equals the total physical capacity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:83
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\sum_{i=1}^{N} w_i = N"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:87
msgid ""
"where *N* represents the number of houses in the system. This constraint "
"ensures energy conservation between the physical battery and the virtual "
"batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:89
msgid ""
"The system implements weight boundaries to ensure fairness and prevent "
"extreme allocations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:91
#, python-brace-format
msgid "w_{min} \\leq w_i \\leq w_{max}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:97
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`w_{min} = \\alpha` (guaranteed minimum weight, typically 0.8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:99
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`w_{max} = 1 + (1 - \\alpha) \\times (N - 1)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:102
msgid "Virtual Battery Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:103
msgid ""
"The virtual battery implements charge and discharge operations that "
"maintain energy conservation across the distributed system. The charge "
"operation accounts for charging efficiency and capacity constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:105
msgid ""
"P_{charge,actual} = \\min\\left(P_{charge} \\times \\eta_{charge} \\times"
" \\Delta t, C_{total} - C_{residual}\\right) \\times \\frac{1}{\\Delta t "
"\\times \\eta_{charge}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:111
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{charge,actual}` represents the actual power consumed for charging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:113
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{charge}` represents the requested charging power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:115
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`\\eta_{charge}` represents the charging efficiency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:117
msgid ""
"`\\Delta t` represents the time interval in hours: `\\Delta t = "
"\\frac{\\Delta t_{s}}{3600}` where `\\Delta t_{s}` represents the time "
"interval in seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:119
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{total}` represents the maximum capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:121
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{residual}` represents the current residual capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:123
msgid ""
"The discharge operation implements efficiency losses and capacity "
"limitations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:125
msgid ""
"P_{discharge,actual} = \\min\\left(\\frac{P_{discharge} \\times \\Delta "
"t}{\\eta_{charge}}, C_{residual}\\right) \\times "
"\\frac{\\eta_{charge}}{\\Delta t}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:129
msgid "The energy conversion between power and capacity uses the relationship:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:131
msgid "E = P \\times \\Delta t"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:135
msgid "where energy is measured in watt-hours and power in watts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:138
msgid "Weight Adjustment Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:139
msgid ""
"The adjustment function modifies weights while maintaining system "
"constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:141
#, python-brace-format
msgid "w_{i}^{t+1} = \\text{clamp}(w_{i}^{t} + \\Delta w_{i}, w_{min}, w_{max})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:145
msgid ""
"After adjusting the weights, the new capacity for the virtual battery is "
"calculated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:147
msgid "C_{vb,i}^{t+1} = \\frac {C_{total}}{N} \\times w_{i}^{t+1}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:151
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When weight adjustment reduces total capacity `C_{vb,i}^{t+1}` below "
"current residual capacity `C_{vb,i}^{residual}`, the excess energy is "
"calculated and returned to the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:153
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E_{excess} = \\max(0, C_{vb,i}^{residual} - C_{vb,i}^{t+1})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:157
msgid ""
"This excess energy is then redistributed among the other virtual "
"batteries to conserve the energy during system optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:160
msgid "Adaptive Learning Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:161
msgid ""
"The power management system implements an adaptive learning algorithm "
"that continuously adjusts virtual battery weights based on consumption. "
"This algorithm enables the system to optimize energy allocation over "
"time, improving efficiency as it learns each house's consumption "
"patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:164
msgid "Load Deviation Calculation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:165
msgid ""
"The learning algorithm employs statistical analysis of houses consumption"
" to make decisions regarding their weights. It begins by calculating "
"deviations from the mean consumption to identify houses with above-"
"average and below-average demand:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:167
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mu_{L} = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} L_{i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:171
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\sigma_{i} = L_i - \\mu_{L}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:177
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`L_{i}` represents the current load for the i-th house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:179
msgid ""
"The deviation values undergo normalization to ensure consistent scaling "
"across different load magnitudes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:181
msgid "\\sigma_{norm,i} = \\frac{\\sigma_{i}}{\\max_j |\\sigma_{j}|}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:185
msgid ""
"This normalization prevents large load values from overwhelming the "
"learning algorithm and ensures that weight adjustments respond "
"proportionally to relative consumption differences rather than absolute "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:188
msgid "Load Redistribution for Minimum Weight Houses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:189
msgid ""
"The algorithm implements a redistribution mechanism for houses operating "
"at a minimum weight. When a house reaches its minimum weight and exhibits"
" below-average consumption, the algorithm redistributes its negative "
"deviation to houses with above-average consumption:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:191
msgid "S_{pos} = \\{i \\mid \\sigma_{i} > 0 \\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:195
msgid "S_{neg} = \\{i \\mid \\sigma_{i} < 0 \\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:199
msgid "S_{min} = \\{i \\mid w_{i} = w_{min} \\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:203
msgid ""
"\\sigma_{norm,j}^{adjusted} = \\sigma_{norm,j} + \\sigma_{norm,i} \\times"
" \\frac{\\sigma_{norm,j}}{\\sum_{k \\in S_{pos}} \\sigma_{norm,k}}, "
"\\quad i \\in S_{min} \\cap S_{neg}, \\; j \\in S_{pos}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:207
msgid ""
"This redistribution maintains energy conservation and ensures that houses"
" at minimum weight do not continue to lose capacity allocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:210
msgid "Weight Update and Learning Step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:211
msgid ""
"The calculated adjustments are then scaled by the learning rate and sent "
"to the virtual battery to calculate its new weight:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:213
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\Delta w_{i}^{t+1} = \\sigma_{norm,i}^{adjusted} \\times "
"\\alpha_{learning}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:217
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where `\\alpha_{learning}` represents the learning rate (typically "
"0.002). The learning rate parameter controls the convergence speed and "
"system stability. Smaller values provide more stable convergence at the "
"cost of slower adaptation, while larger values enable rapid adaptation "
"but may introduce oscillatory behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:219
msgid ""
"The total excess capacity released from all weight adjustments is then "
"aggregated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:221
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E_{excess} = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} E_{excess,i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:225
msgid ""
"This excess capacity becomes available for redistribution during the "
"charging phase, ensuring that energy released through weight reductions "
"does not disappear, thus maintaining energy conservation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:228
msgid "Power Distribution Algorithms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:229
msgid ""
"The power management system implements algorithms for distributing "
"available power sources among connected houses while maintaining fairness"
" and system efficiency. These algorithms coordinate solar panel output, "
"utility grid power, and virtual battery discharge to meet residential "
"demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:232
msgid "Houses Virtual Battery Usage Calculation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:233
msgid ""
"The virtual battery usage calculation determines how much energy each "
"house should draw from their virtual battery after accounting for the "
"solar and utility power available. The algorithm implements a priority-"
"based allocation system that processes houses in ascending order of load "
"demand to ensure fair distribution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:235
msgid ""
"P_{panels,used,i} = \\min\\left(L_i, "
"\\frac{P_{panels,available}}{N_{remaining}}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:239
msgid ""
"P_{utility,used,i} = \\min\\left(L_i - P_{panels,used,i}, "
"\\frac{P_{utility,available}}{N_{remaining}}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:243
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{vb,i} = L_i - P_{panels,used,i} - P_{utility,used,i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:249
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`L_{i}` represents the load of the i-th house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:251
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{panels,available}` represents remaining solar panel power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:253
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{utility,available}` represents remaining utility power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:255
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`N_{remaining}` represents the number of houses not yet processed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:257
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{vb,i}` represents the i-th house power demand from its virtual battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:259
msgid ""
"This sequential allocation ensures that houses with lower demand receive "
"priority access to available solar and utility power, as they might not "
"use their full share, thus allowing for efficient redistribution of the "
"remainder equally among the remaining houses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:262
msgid "Virtual Battery Charging Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:263
msgid ""
"When excess power becomes available from solar generation, the charging "
"algorithm distributes this power among virtual batteries based on their "
"remaining capacity and charging capabilities. The algorithm implements "
"priority charging for batteries with the lowest capacity deficit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:265
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{Charging order: } \\arg\\min_i (C_{total,i} - C_{residual,i})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:269
msgid "The charging power allocation follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:271
msgid "P_{charge,i} = \\frac{P_{charge,available}}{N_{remaining}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:275
msgid ""
"where virtual batteries are processed in order of their capacity deficit,"
" ensuring that batteries with the least available space receive charging "
"priority as they might not need their full share, thus allowing for "
"efficient redistribution of the remainder of their share equally among "
"the remaining virtual batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:278
msgid "Virtual Battery Discharging with Weighted Distribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:279
msgid ""
"The discharging algorithm implements weighted power distribution based on"
" the normalized power demands from the virtual batteries. The algorithm "
"calculates discharge weights using sum normalization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:281
msgid ""
"w_{discharge,i} = \\begin{cases} \\dfrac{P_{vb,i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^{N} "
"P_{vb,j}} & \\sum_{j=1}^{N} P_{vb,j} > \\epsilon \\\\[2ex] \\dfrac{1}{N} "
"& \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:285
msgid ""
"When the denominator approaches zero (no house demands discharging of its"
" virtual battery), the algorithm defaults to equal distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:287
msgid "The actual discharge power for each virtual battery follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:289
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{discharge,i} = P_{discharge,total} \\times w_{discharge,i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:293
msgid ""
"The algorithm tracks whether each virtual battery can fully meet its "
"required discharge:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:295
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{Usage Met} = |P_{discharge,i} - P_{actual,i}| < \\epsilon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:299
msgid ""
"Houses whose virtual batteries cannot meet their full energy requirements"
" trigger load line disconnection to prevent system instability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:302
msgid "System-Wide Load Line Coordination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:303
msgid ""
"The power manager coordinates load line states between individual houses "
"and the solar system inverter. When the inverter implements load shedding"
" due to extreme power shortage, the power manager propagates this state "
"to all connected houses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:305
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\neg LL_{inverter} \\rightarrow \\neg LL_{i}, \\quad \\forall i"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:309
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:331
msgid "where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:311
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`LL_{inverter}` represents the state of the inverter load line connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:313
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`LL_{i}` represents the state of the load line connection of the i-th "
"house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:315
msgid ""
"This ensures individual house load line states remain consistent with "
"overall system capacity and prevents conflicts between local and system-"
"wide load management decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:317
msgid ""
"Restoration operates automatically after a configurable set interval "
"(typically 30 seconds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:320
msgid "Utility Power Export Distribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:321
msgid ""
"The power management system implements an algorithm for distributing "
"utility export power among houses when excess energy becomes available "
"for grid export. The algorithm ensures fair distribution of export "
"benefits while accounting for individual house contributions to system "
"efficiency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:324
msgid "Export Eligibility and Weight Calculation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:325
msgid ""
"The utility export distribution algorithm operates exclusively on houses "
"that maintain active utility line connections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:327
msgid "S_{export} = \\{i \\mid UL_{i} \\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:333
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`UL_{i}` represents the utility line connection state of the i-th house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:335
msgid ""
"The export weight calculation employs inverse virtual battery weights to "
"provide higher export allocation to houses with lower virtual battery "
"weights, creating incentives for efficient energy usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:337
msgid "w_{export,i} = \\frac{1}{w_{vb,i}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:341
msgid ""
"The normalized export distribution calculates each house's share of total"
" export power using sum normalization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:343
msgid ""
"w_{export,norm,i} = \\frac{w_{export,i}}{\\sum_{j \\in S_{export}} "
"w_{export,j}}, \\quad \\forall i \\in S_{export}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:348
msgid "Export Power Allocation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:349
msgid "The final export power allocation for each eligible house follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:351
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{export,i} = P_{export,total} \\times w_{export,norm,i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:355
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where `P_{export,total}` represents the total power available for utility"
" export from the solar system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:357
msgid ""
"This ensures that houses with more efficient virtual battery utilization "
"(lower weights) receive proportionally higher export benefits, creating "
"economic incentives for optimal energy usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:360
msgid "System Integration and Real-Time Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:361
msgid ""
"The power management system maintains continuous coordination with "
"simulation components through real-time interfaces. The integration "
"architecture ensures that power management decisions reflect current "
"system state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:364
msgid "Real-Time Update Cycle Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:365
msgid ""
"The power manager executes its core algorithm within a threaded update "
"loop that operates independently of other system components. The update "
"cycle duration matches the simulation time step, typically configured to "
"100-millisecond intervals. This synchronization ensures that power "
"management decisions occur at the same time as houses simulation and "
"solar system simulation updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:367
msgid ""
"The update sequence implements a structured workflow that processes "
"system state, executes learning algorithms, performs power distribution "
"calculations, and updates component states within each cycle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:406
msgid "Inverter Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:407
msgid ""
"The power manager maintains synchronization with the solar system "
"inverter through bidirectional communication that coordinates load "
"requirements and power delivery capabilities. The synchronization "
"algorithm updates inverter state based on aggregated house demands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:409
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{load,inverter} = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} L_{i} \\times LL_{i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:413
#, python-brace-format
msgid "where `LL_{i}` represents the binary load line state for the i-th house."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:415
msgid ""
"The utility line state coordination ensures that the inverter maintains "
"proper grid connection based on house connectivity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:417
#, python-brace-format
msgid "UL_{inverter} = \\bigvee_{i=1}^{N} UL_{i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:421
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where `UL_{i}` represents the binary utility line state for the i-th "
"house. This coordination maintains consistency between individual house "
"utility connections and overall system grid interface requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:423
msgid ""
"The current model for setting the inverter's utility line is not "
"representative of the real world and thus must be changed to one more "
"closely reflective of reality. It was set as this for now for the lack of"
" a better idea, and further analysis of the problem was precluded by "
"approaching deadlines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:426
msgid "Performance Monitoring and Data Collection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:427
msgid ""
"The power management system implements data collection that captures "
"system performance metrics and algorithm behavior. The monitoring system "
"enables both real-time performance assessment and historical analysis of "
"power management effectiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:429
msgid ""
"The system collects time-series data for all virtual battery states, "
"capturing capacity utilization, weight evolution, and energy flow "
"throughout simulation execution. The collected data enables statistical "
"analysis of algorithm convergence, weight distribution evolution, and "
"system efficiency improvements over time. Performance metrics derived "
"from this data include average utility grid dependence, battery "
"utilization efficiency, and load balancing effectiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:431
msgid ""
"The collected data allows for the calculation of key performance metrics "
"that measure power management effectiveness and system optimization "
"success. Primary metrics include utility grid import minimization and "
"battery capacity utilization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:433
msgid ""
"\\text{Grid Dependence Ratio} = \\frac{\\sum_t "
"P_{utility,import,t}}{\\sum_t P_{load,total,t}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:437
msgid ""
"\\text{Battery Utilization} = \\frac{\\sum_t C_{discharge,t}}{\\sum_t "
"C_{residual,t}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:441
msgid ""
"These metrics provide quantitative assessment of power management "
"performance and enable comparison between different algorithm "
"configurations and parameter settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:443
msgid ""
"The extensive data collection enables future integration of machine "
"learning for predictive algorithms and advanced optimization techniques."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:5
msgid ""
"The dashboard serves as the human-machine interface for the residential "
"smart grid prototype, providing real-time monitoring and control. This "
"chapter examines the implementation of the graphical user interface and "
"the remote object communication architecture that enable operators to "
"interact with the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:8
msgid "Remote Object Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:9
msgid ""
"The dashboard implements a distributed architecture using Pyro5 remote "
"objects to communicate with the simulation components. This design "
"separates the user interface from the computation-intensive simulation "
"processes, enabling the dashboard to run independently while maintaining "
"synchronized access to system state and control functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:11
msgid ""
"The system uses environment variables to configure connection parameters,"
" allowing deployment flexibility across different network configurations "
"and development environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:13
msgid ""
"The Pyro5 remote object framework provides transparent network "
"communication, enabling the dashboard to treat remote simulation "
"components as local objects while maintaining network resilience and "
"error handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:16
msgid "Dashboard Application Framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:17
msgid ""
"The dashboard application builds upon the Tkinter GUI framework enhanced "
"with ttkbootstrap styling to provide a modern, responsive user interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:23
msgid ""
"The application implements a hierarchical view structure that scales to "
"accommodate varying numbers of houses and devices within the simulation. "
"The framework provides scrollable interfaces for scenarios with large "
"numbers of components, ensuring usability regardless of simulation scale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:26
msgid "Houses Simulation Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:27
msgid ""
"The houses simulation interface provides monitoring and control "
"capabilities for individual houses. Each house panel displays current "
"power consumption, connectivity status, and provides access to control "
"the house's load. The utility line and load line toggles enable operators"
" to simulate grid disconnections to support testing of power management "
"response mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:29
msgid ""
"The house control window provides access to individual device operations "
"within each house. These windows display device-specific information "
"including current load and configuration parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:32
msgid "Summary and Monitoring Views"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:33
msgid ""
"The dashboard implements dedicated summary views for each major "
"simulation component, providing comprehensive real-time status "
"information and operational metrics. These views serve as primary "
"monitoring interfaces for system analysis and troubleshooting activities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:35
msgid ""
"The houses simulation summary displays system-wide statistics including "
"total load, individual house contributions, and connectivity states. The "
"information updates continuously during simulation execution and provides"
" formatted output that facilitates rapid assessment of system state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:37
msgid ""
"The solar system simulation summary provides detailed information about "
"photovoltaic generation, battery state, and inverter operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:39
msgid ""
"The power management summary displays algorithm performance metrics and "
"decision-making status. This information proves essential for evaluating "
"power management effectiveness and identifying areas for algorithm "
"improvement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:42
msgid "Real-time Update Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:43
msgid ""
"The dashboard implements a real-time update system that maintains "
"synchronization between the user interface and the underlying simulation."
" The length of the update cycle can be set to balance between maintaining"
" real-time connection and minimizing overhead. As such, the default of "
"100-milliseconds was chosen as a middle between responsiveness and low "
"overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:46
msgid "Data Collection and Analysis Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:47
msgid ""
"The dashboard provides access to simulation data through its summary "
"views and component monitoring interfaces. This information supports both"
" real-time system analysis and post-simulation evaluation of system "
"performance and algorithm effectiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C6_dashboard.rst:49
msgid ""
"The data is currently displayed only as summaries, lacking any "
"visualization, as the goal of the dashboard was to debug the simulation "
"and power management solutions. However, the data exported to CSV files "
"from the various simulation components can be imported into a third party"
" tool for visualization and statistical analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:6
msgid ""
"The Raspberry Pi controller serves as the physical hardware interface for"
" the residential smart grid project. This chapter examines the "
"implementation of the GPIO controller system that bridges the gap between"
" the software simulation and physical hardware controls. The controller "
"enables real-time interaction with the RSGP simulation through physical "
"buttons and visual feedback via LEDs; thus providing an intuitive "
"hardware-in-the-loop testing environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:8
msgid ""
"The significance of the Raspberry Pi controller extends beyond simple "
"input and output operations. It demonstrates the practical application of"
" smart grid control systems in a physical environment. The controller "
"implements a bidirectional communication system that synchronizes "
"hardware state with simulation components. This approach enables "
"researchers to evaluate system behavior under realistic manual "
"intervention scenarios; scenarios that mirror real-world smart grid "
"operations where human operators must interact with automated systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:10
msgid ""
"The Raspberry Pi controller addresses the challenge of validating "
"simulation algorithms in environments where physical interaction proves "
"necessary. Traditional simulation systems operate in isolation; limiting "
"their ability to demonstrate real-world applicability. The controller "
"bridges this gap by providing tactile feedback mechanisms that enable "
"users to understand system responses to manual interventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:13
msgid "System Architecture Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:14
msgid ""
"The Raspberry Pi controller architecture separates hardware abstraction, "
"GPIO management, and simulation integration into distinct layers. This "
"modular design ensures that hardware-specific code remains isolated from "
"simulation logic; thus maintaining system flexibility and enabling future"
" expansion to different hardware platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:55
msgid ""
"The architecture implements a three-layer approach: the hardware layer "
"manages physical GPIO operations; the controller layer provides "
"abstraction and mapping logic; and the communication layer enables remote"
" interaction with the RSGP simulation. This separation ensures that each "
"layer operates independently; thus allowing for individual component "
"testing and modification without affecting other system elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:57
msgid ""
"The modular architecture enables future expansion to support additional "
"hardware platforms by implementing new hardware abstraction layers while "
"maintaining the same controller interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:60
msgid "Hardware Configuration and GPIO Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:61
msgid ""
"The hardware configuration system manages the mapping between physical "
"GPIO pins and logical device controls. The system employs a structured "
"approach to GPIO allocation that ensures consistent hardware layout and "
"prevents pin conflicts between different control elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:64
msgid "GPIO Pin Allocation Strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:65
msgid ""
"The pin allocation follows a systematic approach that groups related "
"controls and maintains logical separation between houses and device "
"types. The allocation strategy ensures that each house receives dedicated"
" GPIO pins for its device controls; while global controls such as the "
"utility line receive separate pin assignments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:95
msgid ""
"The GPIO mapping employs a paired button-LED configuration where each "
"control function receives both an input button and a corresponding output"
" LED. The button enables user interaction; while the LED provides visual "
"feedback about the current state of the associated simulation component. "
"This pairing ensures that users receive immediate confirmation of their "
"actions and continuous state information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:98
msgid "Device Type Enumeration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:99
msgid ""
"The system implements a comprehensive device type enumeration that covers"
" the primary controllable elements within the residential smart grid "
"simulation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:110
msgid ""
"The enumeration provides type safety and ensures consistent device "
"identification across the hardware configuration system. Each device type"
" maps to specific GPIO pins and callback functions; thus enabling "
"targeted control over individual simulation elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:113
msgid "Mathematical GPIO Pin Assignment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:114
msgid ""
"The GPIO pin assignment follows a mathematical pattern that ensures "
"systematic allocation across houses and device types. The button pin "
"allocation for house devices follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:116
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{button,h,d} = (h-1) \\times 4 + d + 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:120
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`h` represents the house number (1-3), :math:`d` represents "
"the device index (0-3), and :math:`P_{button}` represents the assigned "
"button GPIO pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:122
msgid "The LED pin allocation maintains a consistent offset from button pins:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:124
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{LED,h,d} = P_{button,h,d} + 13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:128
msgid ""
"This mathematical relationship ensures predictable pin assignments and "
"simplifies hardware layout planning. The utility line receives dedicated "
"pin assignments outside the house-specific allocation range to prevent "
"conflicts with house-level controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:131
msgid "GPIOController Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:132
msgid ""
"The ``GPIOController`` class serves as the primary interface between the "
"Raspberry Pi hardware and the RSGP simulation system. The controller "
"implements comprehensive GPIO management; including input monitoring; "
"output control; and bidirectional communication with simulation "
"components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:135
msgid "Controller Initialization and Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:136
msgid ""
"The controller initialization process establishes GPIO chip access; "
"configures pin modes; and sets up callback mechanisms for user "
"interactions. The initialization sequence ensures that all hardware "
"resources are properly allocated before beginning the main control loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:147
msgid ""
"The GPIO setup employs pull-up resistors for button inputs to ensure "
"reliable signal detection; while LED outputs initialize to the off state "
"to provide a consistent starting configuration. The controller maintains "
"internal state tracking for both buttons and LEDs to enable efficient "
"change detection and minimize unnecessary GPIO operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:150
msgid "Button State Monitoring Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:151
msgid ""
"The button monitoring system implements edge detection to identify button"
" press events while filtering noise and preventing multiple triggers from"
" single user actions. The algorithm maintains previous button states and "
"compares them with current readings to detect falling edge transitions "
"that indicate button presses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:153
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{Button Press} = S_{previous} \\land \\neg S_{current}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:157
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`S_{previous}` represents the previous button state and "
":math:`S_{current}` represents the current button state. This logical "
"operation identifies the transition from high to low that occurs when a "
"button is pressed with pull-up configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:159
msgid ""
"The button reading cycle operates continuously within the main update "
"loop:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:174
msgid "LED State Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:175
msgid ""
"The LED state synchronization system maintains visual feedback that "
"accurately reflects the current state of simulation components. The "
"synchronization algorithm queries simulation components to determine "
"their current operational status; then updates LED states accordingly to "
"provide real-time visual feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:177
msgid ""
"The LED update process implements efficient change detection to minimize "
"GPIO write operations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:179
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\text{LED Update Required} = S_{LED,cached} \\neq S_{simulation,current}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:183
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`S_{LED,cached}` represents the cached LED state and "
":math:`S_{simulation,current}` represents the current simulation "
"component state. This comparison prevents unnecessary GPIO operations "
"when states remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:186
msgid "Device Control Callback Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:187
msgid ""
"The controller implements specialized callback functions for each device "
"type; ensuring that user interactions trigger appropriate simulation "
"responses. The callback system employs a mapping mechanism that "
"associates GPIO pins with specific control functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:190
msgid "Utility Line Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:191
msgid ""
"The utility line control callback affects all houses simultaneously; "
"reflecting the global nature of utility grid connection in the smart grid"
" system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:200
msgid ""
"This global control mechanism demonstrates the hierarchical nature of "
"smart grid operations where system-wide decisions affect multiple "
"individual components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:203
msgid "Individual Device Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:204
msgid ""
"Individual device controls target specific house devices; enabling fine-"
"grained control over simulation behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C7_rasp_controller.rst:206
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\text{Device Toggle} = f(\\text{house\\_id}, \\text{device\\_type}, "
"\\text{simulation\\_time})"
msgstr ""

